  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know the relation between radius and atomic mass number is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>A</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;<br />It is similar to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;which is equation of line passing through origin.</p>",
